# Curbside Infrastructure Overview

How all the accounts, domains, and services fit together.

---

## The domain

**`curbsidescore.com`** — registered and DNS-managed through **Cloudflare** (nameservers pointed at Cloudflare, all records set to DNS only / grey cloud — proxying is deliberately off everywhere so Vercel and Railway can each issue their own SSL certificates).

| Subdomain | Points to | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `curbsidescore.com` / `www` | Vercel — landing page project | Public marketing site |
| `api.curbsidescore.com` | Railway | Backend API |
| `app.curbsidescore.com` | Vercel — app project | Logged-in "saved evaluations" website |

---

## The four services

### 1. Cloudflare — DNS only
- Owns DNS for `curbsidescore.com`.
- Not used for CDN/proxy/security features — everything is set to "DNS only" on purpose, because Vercel and Railway need to see direct traffic to manage SSL themselves.
- Also hosts DNS records Resend needs for email sending (SPF/DKIM/MX — the `send.`, `resend._domainkey`, and `_railway-verify` type records).

### 2. Vercel — two separate projects, both under the `curbside1` team
- **Landing page project** (dashboard name `usecurbside`, originally `curbsideprod`) — static HTML site. Domains: `curbsidescore.com`, `www.curbsidescore.com`.
- **`curbside-app` project** — Next.js app for the logged-in bookmarks/saved-evaluations feature. Domain: `app.curbsidescore.com`. Calls the Railway backend via API — holds no data itself.
- Kept as two separate projects intentionally: the landing page stays simple/static and isn't coupled to the app's build pipeline or auth system.

### 3. Railway — the backend
- Runs the FastAPI backend (Postgres + API), reachable at `api.curbsidescore.com`.
- Reads `$PORT` dynamically at runtime (not hardcoded).
- Runs `alembic upgrade head` automatically on every deploy/boot — schema migrations apply themselves.
- Environment variables that matter here:
  - `DEAL_RATER_CORS_ORIGINS` — must include `https://app.curbsidescore.com` or the website's API calls fail with CORS errors.
  - `DEAL_RATER_SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN` — set to `.curbsidescore.com` so the auth cookie works across the `app.` subdomain.
  - `DEAL_RATER_RESEND_API_KEY` — required for magic-link sign-in emails to send; without it, sign-in returns 503.

### 4. Resend — transactional email
- Sends the magic-link sign-in emails for the website.
- Domain `curbsidescore.com` verified there via DNS records (added in Cloudflare).
- Requires: verified domain status + a valid API key in Railway's env vars + the "from" address in the backend code matching the verified domain. A 403 from Resend usually means one of those three is off.

