## The extension

- Chrome Web Store listing (currently unlisted).
- `manifest.json`'s `host_permissions` points at `api.curbsidescore.com` (updated from the original Railway-only URL in version 0.1.3).
- **Any change to `host_permissions` requires publishing a new version to the Chrome Web Store** — existing installs don't pick up a backend URL change until the update ships and Chrome auto-updates the install (Chrome checks for updates periodically, not instantly; can be forced via `chrome://extensions` → Developer mode → Update).
- Saves are stored via the Railway backend, tied to a user's account (magic-link auth), and readable on `app.curbsidescore.com`.

---

## How a request actually flows

**Evaluating a listing:**
Extension (on Facebook Marketplace) → Railway API (`api.curbsidescore.com`) → Postgres + NHTSA + one cached LLM call → result rendered in the extension overlay.

**Saving an evaluation:**
Extension → Railway API stores a serialized snapshot of the evaluation, tied to the signed-in user (or prompts sign-in if not authenticated).

**Signing in:**
User enters email (extension or `app.curbsidescore.com`) → Railway API → Resend sends a magic-link/code → user verifies → Railway issues a session (cookie for the website, token for the extension, stored in `chrome.storage.local`).

**Viewing saved evaluations:**
`app.curbsidescore.com` (Vercel) → Railway API (`GET /users/me/saved`) → returns stored JSON snapshots directly — no re-evaluation, no LLM call, no NHTSA lookup on read.

